# FPMS-OS WiFi setup   -   ROVER 1
#
# YOU PROBABLY DO NOT NEED THIS FILE.
#
# This image already has the competition network baked in:
#
#     FPMS_Net
#
# so a freshly flashed card joins it with no boot-partition file at all. That
# default lives in /etc/fpms/config.env inside the image, not out here, because
# this partition is FAT and every Windows machine mounts it automatically.
#
# USE THIS FILE TO ADD OR PREFER A DIFFERENT NETWORK.
#
# RENAME IT TO  fpms-wifi.conf  (drop the .example) AND EDIT IT.
#
# One network per line:      SSID:PASSWORD
# Order matters - the first line is tried first.
# Lines starting with # are ignored. Blank lines are ignored.
#
# THIS FILE WINS. Everything you list here is registered at a HIGHER
# NetworkManager autoconnect priority than the baked-in FPMS_Net, which is
# appended last. So this file adds to the built-in network rather than
# competing with it, and you never have to re-list FPMS_Net to keep it.
#
# Put your Windows Mobile Hotspot FIRST. The rover's telemetry link expects the
# operator laptop to be on 192.168.137.1, which is what that hotspot uses.
# FPMS_Net is a venue network and will NOT put the laptop on that subnet, so if
# you are working off a hotspot, list it here.
#
# For an open network with no password, leave the part after the colon empty:
#     OpenNetwork:
#
# Once the rover has read this it renames the file to .applied and locks it,
# so your password is not left in plain text on a card any computer can mount.

MyMobileHotspot:changeme
MyHomeWiFi:changeme
